SUMMARY:FreeOnFriday? Nottingham Lots 24R
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\nRIDE LEADER: Jan Zerfoss\
 , average pace 12-13 mph.\nCue and Ride with GPS link: [Nottingham Lots](h
 ttps://ridewithgps.com/routes/55509083)\n**Be Safe\, Have Fun\, and Ride T
 ogether**\n\nThis is a casual ride and the ride leader will ride at the ad
 vertised pace. For this out-of-area ride the group should stay together th
 e entire time (although somewhat strung out as per usual safety and best r
 iding practice) since nobody is familiar with the area or the route. Nobod
 y will get dropped.\n\nBackground and historical information about the Not
 tingham Lots and Brick Meeting:\n[Nottingham Lots](https://nottinghambrick
 .org/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/2018/10/Nottingham-Lots-Brochure.pdf) Our 
 bike route is based on parts of the driving tour shown in this document.\n
 [more about Nottingham Lots](https://www.risingsunmd.org/department/divisi
 on.php?structureid=54)\nSome of you will not be surprised to learn that Ja
 n has ancestral ties to this area. :)\n\nJan will be travelling from Gap P
 A along route 41 south to Calvert Regional Park in Cecil County MD . If an
 yone is interested in travelling that way and wants to meet and caravan fr
 om Gap please contact Jan to make arrangements. Also\, if anybody wants to
  carpool with me I can take one extra passenger and one bike. Others of yo
 u coming from different directions may also want to arrange to caravan and
 /or carpool.\n\nThere are usually multiple portable toilets at the Calvert
  Regional Park parking areas.\n\nWaterfront post-ride refreshments/lunch a
 t [Nauti Goose](https://www.nautigoose.net) 200 W Cherry St\, North East\,
  MD. It is about 9 miles south of Calvert Regional Park - about a 15 minut
 e drive.\n\nIf needed\, first rain date will be Monday June 22\, second ra
 in date Thursday June 25.\n.\nHelmets are mandatory. No earbuds. Please br
 ing water and a basic repair kit (spare tube\, tire levers\, pump/CO2 infl
 ator).\n\nTo eliminate passing around a pen and paper waiver\, we require 
 LBC Club membership and Meetup RSVP below to join this ride. Being on\nMee
 tup does not mean you are a club member. Join here [Member Signup](https:/
 /www.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148)\n\nYour
  RSVP is your agreement to abide by the club's Code of Conduct: [Code of C
 onduct](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=
 257148&module_id=323984)\n\nGuidance if an incident occurs: [Incident Acti
 ons](https://lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148&
 module_id=326137)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-bicycle-club/events/3151228
 18/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260605T192605Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260605T192605Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
