SUMMARY:All Class Club Ride (Long) LC Terre Hill (43R)
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Bicycle Club (LBC) Meetup\n***Be Safe\, Have Fun\, a
 nd Ride Together***\n\nThis is the June All Club Ride Long for the A and B
  rides. Following the ride\, please join us at [Bierhall](https://www.bier
 hallbrewing.com/hours-and-location) which opens at noon for food\, drinks 
 and fellowship\n\nRoute: [https://routes.lancasterbikeclub.net/cue/lc-terr
 e-hill-43r/](https://routes.lancasterbikeclub.net/cue/lc-terre-hill-43r/)\
 n\nThe ride leader will ride at the advertised average speed for the [Ride
  Classifications](https://lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&cl
 ub_id=257148&module_id=325156). This is intended to be a group ride with a
  no-drop rule as the main goal. The ride leader will do his/her best to ke
 ep the group together with occasional regroupings and a sweeper may also b
 e appointed at the start.\nPlease do not join this ride if you are not wil
 ling to ride with the group. If you exceed the posted pace\, you will be r
 iding by yourself and encouraged to join a faster group. If maintaining th
 e advertised average pace is beyond your current ability level\, please co
 nsider joining a slower ride first.\n\nHelmets are mandatory. No earbuds. 
 Please bring water and a basic repair kit (spare tube\, tire levers\, pump
 /CO2 inflator).\n\nTo eliminate passing around a pen and paper waiver\, we
  require LBC Club membership and Meetup RSVP below to join this ride. Bein
 g on Meetup does not mean you are a club member.\nJoin here [Member Signup
 ](https://www.lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=60&club_id=257148
 )\nYour RSVP is your agreement to abide by the club's Code of Conduct: [Co
 de of Conduct](https://lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_
 id=257148&module_id=323984)\nGuidance if an incident occurs: [Incident Act
 ions](https://lancasterbikeclub.net/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=257148
 &module_id=326137)
